✔ Cleaner architecture



====================================================
11. FACTORY METHOD vs SIMPLE FACTORY
====================================================



SIMPLE FACTORY:

Example:


Factory::create(type)



Implementation:


if(type == CAR)

    return new Car();


else if(type == BIKE)

    return new Bike();



Characteristics:

- Single factory class.
- Uses if/else or switch.
- Easy initially.
- Adding new types modifies factory.
- Not fully OCP compliant.



----------------------------------------------------



FACTORY METHOD:


Characteristics:

- Uses inheritance.
- Factory interface is defined.
- Each concrete factory creates one product.
- Adding new products requires adding new factory.
- Existing code remains unchanged.
- Better OCP compliance.



====================================================
12. SIMPLE FACTORY vs FACTORY METHOD EXAMPLE
====================================================


Simple Factory:


Client

 |

Factory

 |

if(type)

 |

